{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27102595","formula":"C₆H₁₄N₂O","hill":"C6H14N2O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":14.0,"N":2.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"N-acetylputrescine"},"descriptions":{"en":"N-Acetylputrescine (NacPut), also known as monoacetylputrescine, is an endogenous metabolite of putrescine and a precursor and metabolic intermediate in the biosynthesis of γ-aminobutyric acid (GABA) from putrescine. The metabolic pathway is specifically putrescine into N-acetylputrescine by putrescine acetyltransferase (PAT), N-acetylputrescine into N-acetyl-γ-aminobutyraldehyde (N-acetyl-GABAL or N-acetyl-GABA aldehyde) by monoamine oxidase B (MAO-B), N-acetyl-GABAL into N-acetyl-γ-aminobutyric acid (N-acetyl-GABA) by aldehyde dehydrogenase (ALDH), and N-acetyl-GABA into GABA by an unknown deacetylase enzyme."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":122356,"mass":130.19,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(=O)NCCCCN","inchikey":"KLZGKIDSEJWEDW-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N-(4-aminobutyl)acetamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"122356","atoms":23,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.63,"y":0.437,"z":-1.063,"el":"O"},{"x":1.224,"y":0.056,"z":0.754,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.919,"y":-1.077,"z":-0.021,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.776,"y":1.133,"z":-0.205,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.748,"y":0.067,"z":0.316,"el":"C"},{"x":0.462,"y":1.272,"z":0.677,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.02,"y":-0.046,"z":-0.526,"el":"C"},{"x":2.249,"y":-0.261,"z":-0.127,"el":"C"},{"x":2.898,"y":-1.581,"z":0.195,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.475,"y":0.876,"z":-1.228,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.288,"y":2.101,"z":-0.252,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.247,"y":-0.909,"z":0.335,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.021,"y":0.305,"z":1.353,"el":"H"},{"x":1.102,"y":2.07,"z":0.285,"el":"H"},{"x":0.175,"y":1.544,"z":1.698,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.548,"y":0.913,"z":-0.529,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.757,"y":-0.278,"z":-1.565,"